build: 2026-06-26 v10.76.28 (Diagnostics that tell a story — launch breadcrumbs)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.27. Diagnostics fix: the shared diagnostic log used to show only
  "launch" because the STARTUP steps logged via os_log, not breadcrumbs — so if a launch
  ever died in the crash-prone window (audio-graph build / voice attach / engine start),
  the log gave no clue WHERE. Now every milestone drops a breadcrumb:
    launch → init done → startup 1/4 (graph) → 2/4 (attach voices) → 3/4 (start engine)
    → 3/4 started OK → 4/4 core ready → confirmed healthy
  A launch that fails stops at the last good breadcrumb, naming the phase — so the
  Safe-Mode recovery log (10.76.26) is now actually actionable. Best-effort file appends
  on the main thread at startup; nothing on the audio thread.
  Test: 10.76.28 launches normally? Tap "Diagnostics" (Compose footer) → you should now
  see the full startup story, not just "launch".
